WEBVTT

00:05.572 --> 00:11.169
Dareni mo mienu deshou

00:13.079 --> 00:18.574
Me o tojite kimi o omou

00:19.285 --> 00:24.723
Itsuka de au

00:25.391 --> 00:31.557
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:31.898 --> 00:38.235
Watashi no kono me ni haru o misete

00:38.538 --> 00:44.602
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:45.078 --> 00:50.880
Sayonara fuyu no machi

00:51.684 --> 00:57.953
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:58.191 --> 01:04.460
Watashi no kokoro ni haru o yonde

01:04.898 --> 01:10.962
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

01:11.237 --> 01:17.335
Sayonara yukitachi yo

01:37.263 --> 01:39.697
The weather is currently fair
and beautiful in Tokyo...

01:39.833 --> 01:44.804
But overcast skies are moving in,
and we can expect rain by this evening.

01:44.804 --> 01:45.405
- Yume-chan...

01:45.405 --> 01:46.235
- Yume-chan...
- Yes?

01:46.773 --> 01:48.536
We'll take the day off today.

01:49.709 --> 01:50.698
Yes?

01:51.077 --> 01:53.443
We don't have any
rush requests today.

01:53.613 --> 01:54.875
So... a day off.

01:56.749 --> 01:57.545
Right!

01:58.017 --> 02:02.477
A Summer Night and a Mage

02:06.559 --> 02:09.357
The day off today.
Where shall I go?

02:10.263 --> 02:12.298
Hello! Oyamada-san!

02:12.298 --> 02:13.099
Huh?

02:13.099 --> 02:14.657
Where's good ol' Oyamada?

02:15.034 --> 02:18.936
Good ol' Oyamada? Do you need
something from my teacher?

02:19.172 --> 02:23.509
He's out all day today. It's his day off.
That's why the office is closed.

02:23.509 --> 02:24.373
Oh.

02:25.178 --> 02:26.975
Shall I take your name?

02:27.247 --> 02:32.844
When you ask someone her name, you
should introduce yourself first, right lady?

02:33.186 --> 02:37.885
Oh, you're right. I'm Trainee
Kikuchi Yume. Nice to meet you.

02:38.791 --> 02:40.656
My name's Morikawa Runa.

02:41.594 --> 02:45.621
If good ol' Oyamada's not here,
then, oh, well. Ok, see ya'!

02:48.067 --> 02:49.432
Native Tokyoite?

02:56.843 --> 02:57.744
This... this!

02:57.744 --> 03:01.976
You mean that e-mail the other day?
I can't believe it!

03:06.119 --> 03:10.613
Shimo-Kitazawa
Shopping Street

03:30.576 --> 03:33.875
Super Market

03:39.319 --> 03:40.616
- Oh! Yume!
- Kera-san!

03:42.588 --> 03:43.289
Here!

03:43.289 --> 03:45.348
No, no. You, please.

03:46.960 --> 03:48.428
Shall I buy it for you?

03:48.428 --> 03:51.920
Oh, no. I wouldn't dare ask
a man to buy me clothes.

03:53.566 --> 03:54.692
What does that mean?

03:58.771 --> 04:02.298
So, not only is the office closed,
but the bar's closed today, too.

04:02.976 --> 04:07.470
He does this every year at this time.
It's not even a regular holiday.

04:07.547 --> 04:12.746
Oyamada-sensei works day and
night. I wonder when he takes a break.

04:13.286 --> 04:16.119
Owner doesn't sleep or eat much.

04:16.255 --> 04:17.882
He'll make himself sick.

04:18.925 --> 04:21.127
Maybe that's what he wants.

04:21.127 --> 04:22.151
What?

04:24.530 --> 04:27.590
I'm gonna get going.
Take your time eating that.

04:27.900 --> 04:29.060
Kera-san!

04:29.102 --> 04:29.932
Huh?

04:30.303 --> 04:32.237
Do you know of a place
nearby with a sandbox?

04:33.806 --> 04:35.239
A sandbox?

04:35.274 --> 04:35.875
"School Grounds Open to Public"

04:35.875 --> 04:37.610
"School Grounds Open to Public"
I wanted to add some sand
to the indoor plants in our office...

04:37.610 --> 04:41.046
I wanted to add some sand
to the indoor plants in our office...

04:44.517 --> 04:45.541
What are you doing?

04:47.120 --> 04:49.455
I'm just taking a
little bit of sand.

04:49.455 --> 04:50.890
Go ahead and take
as much as you want...

04:50.890 --> 04:52.959
Well, I wish I could say that...

04:52.959 --> 04:56.292
But sand is part of school property.
So, keep it down, ok?

04:56.462 --> 05:00.600
I see! I'm sorry.
I was stealing...

05:00.600 --> 05:04.627
Oh, no, don't take me so seriously!
If you only take a little, it's ok.

05:05.405 --> 05:06.235
Bye now!

05:06.806 --> 05:08.205
I'm so sorry.

05:15.815 --> 05:16.873
Hey, wait!

05:18.651 --> 05:20.881
Yasuyuki!
Running away is cowardly!

05:21.487 --> 05:22.784
Leave me alone!

05:25.992 --> 05:28.893
Native Tokyoite... Runa-chan...

05:29.062 --> 05:31.530
"Ice"

05:31.798 --> 05:36.497
Uh-huh! Ok, I got it.
Talk to ya' later.

05:37.904 --> 05:42.603
That was from Osamu.
Fukui-sensei's at school, he said.

05:42.809 --> 05:44.902
So, what are you
gonna do, Mage?

05:45.244 --> 05:46.233
Me?

05:47.113 --> 05:48.648
That one.

05:48.648 --> 05:51.082
You can use Special Power?

05:52.752 --> 05:56.779
Unbelievable. He kept it from us all
this time, that he has Special Power!

05:59.125 --> 06:02.328
Well, people would say I used
Special Power any time I had a success.

06:02.328 --> 06:06.025
People would say I cheated on
everything by using Special Power.

06:07.500 --> 06:10.162
I don't like Special Power at all!

06:13.906 --> 06:16.067
I don't like Special Power at all!

06:20.746 --> 06:26.452
I don't want Special Power, because
people will say I use it on everything...

06:26.452 --> 06:28.454
Let them say
whatever they want.

06:28.454 --> 06:31.691
But that comment about me
not being human is unforgivable!

06:31.691 --> 06:34.251
Yume, don't pay attention
to what they say.

06:35.027 --> 06:38.121
Junko, you just don't
understand... how I feel.

06:38.631 --> 06:40.565
That's right.
I don't understand.

06:40.700 --> 06:44.871
But, Yume, you were
born with the Power.

06:44.871 --> 06:47.807
There's nothing you can
do about it, that Power.

06:47.807 --> 06:50.042
Whether you make the best
of Special Power is up to you, Yume.

06:50.042 --> 06:51.310
Will you use it reluctantly?

06:51.310 --> 06:53.744
Or will you believe it's actually
wonderful and use it willingly?

06:53.880 --> 06:56.415
Keep your chin up!
Stand tall.

06:56.415 --> 06:58.451
Use your Power with pride.

06:58.451 --> 07:00.920
If someone tries to pick a fight with
you when you've done nothing wrong,

07:00.920 --> 07:02.722
I'll take them on in your place.

07:02.722 --> 07:03.916
Junko...

07:04.490 --> 07:09.553
Special Power is wonderful.
That's what Yume always says...

07:15.668 --> 07:20.435
Did you get in a fight because Yasuyuki
kept his Special Power secret from you?

07:22.041 --> 07:23.941
Because it's a lunar
eclipse tonight...

07:25.845 --> 07:31.317
We and Fukui-sensei, our homeroom teacher,
promised we'd moon watch together tonight.

07:31.317 --> 07:34.820
He says he has to quit school
because of a family matter.

07:34.820 --> 07:39.689
So this is our last chance
to watch the sky together.

07:41.460 --> 07:45.123
But the weather forecast said
it's going to rain tonight...

07:45.898 --> 07:47.333
That's why I went...

07:47.333 --> 07:49.824
To request a Special Power
to "clear the sky" tonight.

07:50.570 --> 07:52.572
That's why you
came this morning...

07:52.572 --> 07:55.908
But Yasuyuki kept saying we can't
make a request out of the blue,

07:55.908 --> 07:59.278
and that Special Power used to
manipulate nature are hard to perform.

07:59.278 --> 08:00.713
He knew so much detail.

08:00.713 --> 08:05.184
I made him tell why, and he said
he was a mage! What a surprise!

08:05.184 --> 08:06.652
I didn't want to tell you.

08:06.652 --> 08:10.456
Unwilling to help!
Stingy!

08:10.456 --> 08:13.016
Easy to say for a non-mage.

08:13.459 --> 08:16.929
I've never been able to use my
Power the way I want to.

08:16.929 --> 08:19.632
So how do you expect me
to use such a grand power?

08:19.632 --> 08:23.068
What really makes me mad is that
you've already given up without trying!

08:23.236 --> 08:26.467
I already told you I don't
like Special Power at all!

08:27.607 --> 08:30.041
Mages who don't like
Special Power are...

08:31.210 --> 08:36.512
Mages who don't like Special Power are...
disliked by the Power, too.

08:38.050 --> 08:42.350
Can you use a Special Power
tonight to clear the sky?

08:43.956 --> 08:45.391
I've never used one.

08:45.391 --> 08:49.191
But Special Power to manipulate
nature has too much impact...

08:49.262 --> 08:53.494
Never mind!
Even mages can't do everything!

08:53.799 --> 08:56.927
Boy!
What a bunch of whimps!

08:57.336 --> 08:58.530
Runa-chan!

09:10.316 --> 09:12.307
Why are you hesitating?

09:13.286 --> 09:17.052
What's wrong with using
Special Power to help others?

09:18.024 --> 09:20.760
No mage action without a request!

09:20.760 --> 09:24.890
It's common sense,
Trainee Kikuchi Yume!

09:48.120 --> 09:52.992
Yasuyuki-kun, who's the
mage in your family?

09:52.992 --> 09:54.789
Only my late grandfather.

09:55.594 --> 09:57.863
What about your
mother and father?

09:57.863 --> 09:59.160
They're not mages.

09:59.732 --> 10:00.721
Is that so?

10:04.937 --> 10:06.336
I'm going home.

10:06.639 --> 10:08.504
But what about
your moon watching?

10:10.343 --> 10:12.709
But... I...

10:13.145 --> 10:17.013
But isn't it your last chance
to observe with your teacher?

10:20.619 --> 10:25.022
But, I can't use
Special Power very well.

10:25.891 --> 10:30.521
For my teacher...
I wanted to do something...

10:31.897 --> 10:33.728
Wait, Yasuyuki-kun!

10:36.736 --> 10:39.872
Did you really mean
what you just said?

10:39.872 --> 10:43.774
Do you really want to do
something for your teacher?

10:45.578 --> 10:47.011
Yeah...

11:02.194 --> 11:03.388
Understood.

11:37.596 --> 11:39.530
Well, I wonder how
it's going to be tonight.

11:40.332 --> 11:42.101
If we could only get
a break in the clouds...

11:42.101 --> 11:46.472
Like Osamu says, as long as it doesn't
rain, we'll get a break in the clouds.

11:46.472 --> 11:47.370
Is that right?

11:48.574 --> 11:49.666
Yes, that's right.

11:54.013 --> 11:55.047
Yasuyuki.

11:55.047 --> 11:55.706
You're late.

11:56.482 --> 11:57.779
Sorry.

11:58.050 --> 12:01.144
Can I watch the sky with you?

12:02.988 --> 12:04.319
And you are?

12:04.590 --> 12:05.955
Nice to meet you.

12:06.292 --> 12:08.590
Actually not, huh?
My name's Kikuchi.

12:09.061 --> 12:10.858
I'm a mage.

12:11.297 --> 12:12.628
Just like Yasuyuki-kun.

12:13.232 --> 12:14.961
Just like Yasuyuki?

12:15.901 --> 12:17.069
Absolutely.

12:17.069 --> 12:19.697
But nothing was mentioned in
the Family Information Form.

12:19.872 --> 12:21.965
I hear his grandfather was a mage.

12:23.042 --> 12:27.546
Is that so?
But why didn't you tell me?

12:27.546 --> 12:28.342
I...

12:32.218 --> 12:36.222
You'll use a Special Power tonight?
For me?

12:36.222 --> 12:36.688
Yes.

12:38.390 --> 12:43.555
Thank you, everyone, but I'm
perfectly happy just being with you all.

12:43.996 --> 12:46.065
I knew you'd say that.

12:46.065 --> 12:48.701
We know you don't like to impose.

12:48.701 --> 12:50.931
Did you pressure Yasuyuki?

12:51.303 --> 12:53.237
- Oh, no! Not at all!
- Oh, no! Not at all!

12:55.274 --> 12:59.574
I'm sorry, Yasuyuki,
for burdening you like this.

12:59.778 --> 13:00.574
I'm sorry.

13:01.380 --> 13:02.369
Sensei...

13:03.215 --> 13:04.113
Sensei...

13:04.750 --> 13:06.115
Fukui-sensei...

13:11.824 --> 13:14.452
Yasuyuki-kun, what's wrong?

13:16.028 --> 13:17.791
I... I can't.

13:18.330 --> 13:20.798
I don't want to
disappoint my teacher!

13:26.005 --> 13:30.101
If I fail, no one will
like me anymore.

13:32.211 --> 13:35.942
People don't dislike
someone who's done his best.

13:42.655 --> 13:46.292
Let's give it a try for
your favorite teacher.

13:46.292 --> 13:48.351
I'll help you.

13:52.598 --> 13:56.762
I asked Yume-san to help me,
but I'll still do my best.

13:57.503 --> 13:59.300
Yasuyuki! Cool!

13:59.605 --> 14:00.697
That's the spirit!

14:01.740 --> 14:02.729
Mm!

14:21.226 --> 14:22.523
It's raining!

14:31.103 --> 14:32.838
Hey, I'm coming!
Over here, over here!

14:32.838 --> 14:36.330
I love recess!
Hey, let's play over here!

14:47.386 --> 14:48.683
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

15:01.934 --> 15:03.869
- This is my best masterpiece!

15:03.869 --> 15:04.563
- This is my best masterpiece!
- Hmm...

15:43.308 --> 15:44.410
That's right.

15:44.410 --> 15:47.868
With all your precious feelings
in your heart...

16:15.474 --> 16:16.839
- Ahh!
- Ahh!

16:46.071 --> 16:47.470
Whoooa!

16:58.217 --> 17:00.481
Uh... This is...

17:01.286 --> 17:02.981
The moon!

17:03.222 --> 17:05.924
The moon!
It's the moon?

17:05.924 --> 17:07.357
Awesome, Yasuyuki!

17:07.926 --> 17:09.120
Impossible!

17:09.695 --> 17:12.289
You did it!
You're incredible!

17:23.675 --> 17:24.903
- Cheers!
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

17:31.049 --> 17:35.008
I remembered what we talked
about with you in the classroom.

17:35.320 --> 17:39.416
That's right! My dream was
to have a drink on the moon!

17:49.935 --> 17:52.130
Ewe! Still yucky!

17:52.571 --> 17:53.839
- What's the matter?

17:53.839 --> 17:55.534
- What's the matter?
- Cool, huh?

17:56.175 --> 17:57.802
Want some more?

18:07.886 --> 18:10.656
Affirmative. No report of
a Grand Mage Action.

18:10.656 --> 18:13.692
What?
Something's wrong with the moon?

18:13.692 --> 18:15.527
Check the ID's of
all mages in action!

18:15.527 --> 18:18.826
We have not verified that it
was the result of mage action.

18:19.398 --> 18:22.034
You're trying to blame
everything on mage action.

18:22.034 --> 18:26.266
Even if it were by mage action,
it can't be a mage from our country.

18:27.039 --> 18:30.770
What's that?
Master Chief's not in right now.

18:31.310 --> 18:35.872
Yes. Therefore, Mr. Chief Spokesman,
an international situation is...

18:46.258 --> 18:49.795
Yume-san, thank you
for your Special Power.

18:49.795 --> 18:53.265
Oh, no, Yasuyuki.
You took us there.

18:53.265 --> 18:57.599
I could feel it.
You helped me out.

18:57.769 --> 19:00.294
Yes, but you're
certainly a mage, too.

19:02.107 --> 19:05.304
I should've put in an
official request, right?

19:08.547 --> 19:12.108
Will you get in trouble?
Will they punish you?

19:12.484 --> 19:15.351
I'll be fine.
It won't be too bad.

19:15.988 --> 19:18.013
Tell them it was my fault!

19:18.156 --> 19:19.350
Your fault?

19:19.658 --> 19:23.594
Since I'm not a
full-fledged mage yet...

19:23.862 --> 19:27.332
If we say I did it all...

19:27.332 --> 19:29.801
I would never blame
it on anyone else.

19:29.801 --> 19:30.392
What?

19:30.469 --> 19:35.133
If anyone asks what
happened today, I'll tell the truth.

19:35.440 --> 19:38.911
I'll say it was my responsibility
in using my Special Power...

19:38.911 --> 19:43.211
and that I used it as
best I could with pride.

19:43.548 --> 19:45.015
That's what I'll say.

19:48.587 --> 19:52.891
Watching you and your friends
reminded me of my friends.

19:52.891 --> 19:54.654
We had fun today, didn't we?

19:54.826 --> 19:55.928
Yume-san?

19:55.928 --> 19:56.792
Yes?

19:57.262 --> 20:01.722
I still don't like
Special Power much, but...

20:03.502 --> 20:06.699
I'll never forget
what happened tonight.

20:09.942 --> 20:12.410
I won't ever forget, either.

20:20.886 --> 20:22.285
There is no problem.

20:22.554 --> 20:24.522
I've already taken care of it.

20:25.390 --> 20:26.792
But what should I do
about the media?

20:26.792 --> 20:29.561
They're already
making a big fuss on TV.

20:29.561 --> 20:32.724
Don't do a thing.
There will be no official comment, either.

20:32.965 --> 20:34.432
But, Master Chief...

20:34.533 --> 20:35.727
That will be all.

21:20.112 --> 21:26.642
Furikaereba ima demo soko ni

21:29.621 --> 21:35.821
Oikaketeta mirai ga atta

21:37.896 --> 21:46.998
Boku no kokoro ni aru taisetsu na mono

21:47.139 --> 21:51.769
Mada mienai ao to

21:52.677 --> 21:59.606
Nagareru kumo ni negatta

22:02.387 --> 22:04.446
Under the Blue Sky

22:04.723 --> 22:11.754
Ano hi bokura ga egaita yume kara

22:11.863 --> 22:18.598
Samenai you ni tomaranai you ni

22:21.373 --> 22:23.398
Under the Blue Sky

22:23.675 --> 22:30.513
Kagayaki nagara aruiteikou yo

22:30.682 --> 22:36.678
Owaranai tabi wa tsuzuku

22:49.434 --> 22:51.902
PREVIEW

22:52.204 --> 22:54.539
Well, how'd you like the love story
of me and good ol' Oyamada?

22:54.539 --> 22:55.774
Next week's episode is...

22:55.774 --> 23:00.011
Excuse me, Pip Squeak,
but Masami-chan's mine, all mine!

23:00.011 --> 23:01.279
And I won't let
anyone take him!

23:01.279 --> 23:05.317
Big Sis! Long time no see!
Taking a break from spinning dishes?

23:05.317 --> 23:08.620
I don't spin dishes! I'm a DJ.
How many times do I need to tell you?

23:08.620 --> 23:09.821
- You just do that on purpose!

23:09.821 --> 23:11.123
- You just do that on purpose!
- No way!

23:11.123 --> 23:13.557
In the next episode,
Big Sis and I make a spectacular showing!

23:13.625 --> 23:15.627
An Apron and Champagne
Episode Five is
"An Apron and Champagne."

23:15.627 --> 23:17.229
An Apron and Champagne
I hope you look forward to it!

23:17.229 --> 23:19.322
An Apron and Champagne
Um... What about me?
